Each extension must be attached to the border leaf, in `DEPLOYED`, and its
`extensionValues` must carry the declared interface, dot1q tag and neighbour
address. The three "seen" columns are substring matches against that field,
which Nexus Dashboard returns as a JSON document encoded into a string.

A whole row reading `NO` with state `absent` almost always means stage 02 ran
after stage 05: the create role uses `state: replaced` against a model that
deliberately omits the border leaf, so it detaches every extension. Re-run
`05_vrf_lite.yml`. A row that is attached and `DEPLOYED` but has a `NO` in one
of the seen columns means the extension exists with different values than
`dc_vrf_lite.yml` declares - someone edited it in the UI, or the controller
allocated its own addresses because the declared ones were removed.

