## Not covered by this report

- **The edge router's side of the VRF-Lite links.** The extensions on
  DC-Service-Leaf are built by `05_vrf_lite.yml` and checked above, but the
  matching sub-interfaces and BGP neighbours on DC-SITE11-CEDGE8Kv are not.
  The External fabric is in Monitor Mode, so Nexus Dashboard never writes to
  that router and has nothing to report about it. Its side of the three links
  is pre-built by the pod, which is why the addresses in `dc_vrf_lite.yml`
  are pinned rather than allocated.
- **BGP adjacency state.** That the extension is `DEPLOYED` means the
  controller pushed it, not that the neighbour came up.
- **Data plane.** This is an intent-versus-controller comparison. It proves
  Nexus Dashboard deployed what was declared; it does not prove a server on
  MainNetwork1 can reach one on ProdNetwork1.
